Fri Oct 23 07:09:35 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.13.0 (upstream tag v0.13.0, 2026-10-23):
  * 0.13.0: recover existing macOS PDF associations (no Linux
    change).
  * Forms: Prepare a form gains Calculation order and Text field
    table pages; renaming a field updates the calculations reading
    it; tooltips on hover; arrow keys nudge the selected field.
  * Editing: Edit and Format text panels relaid out, one editing
    session per paragraph; rotate images by any angle; Header &
    Footer in Times or Courier; Ctrl+V pastes a picture; fills and
    border widths for text boxes and callouts.
  * Viewer: optional gapless continuous display; full screen shows
    one fitted page at a time; thumbnail size controls; Layers
    panel reset; Print keeps the printer and paper size.
  * Organize: reverse page order, Ctrl-drag copies pages, custom
    document properties; Save As writes a clean copy, saves keep
    file permissions and creation date.
  * Rendering (patched hayro crates): /DefaultGray/RGB/CMYK,
    knockout groups, stencil masks, JP2 palettes, mesh seams,
    clip-only text extraction, Japanese CID spacing; hayro-cmap is
    now vendored and patched for tolerant CMap parsing.
  * New interface languages: Albanian, Catalan, Central Kurdish,
    Finnish, Hindi, Indonesian, Korean, Lao, Norwegian Bokmal,
    Romanian, Thai; Czech, French, Portuguese (BR), Polish and
    Spanish catalogs completed.
  * Security hardening (no CVE ids): encryption and signature
    validation gaps closed, copy/print/removal limits enforced,
    redaction removes hidden content completely or refuses, parser
    and export work bounded, CSV formulas neutralised, recovery
    folder owner-only on Unix; rustls-webpki 0.103.16
    (RUSTSEC-2026-0382).
  * Many redaction, XFA, FormCalc, text-extraction and save fixes;
    date handling now goes through chrono.
  * Re-vendored (update=false kept for --locked): in the shipped
    graph only rustls-webpki 0.103.15 -> 0.103.16 (ISC) changed and
    hayro-cmap 0.1.0 moved from crates.io to upstream's patched
    vendor/ copy (Apache-2.0 OR MIT, same BSD-3-Clause Adobe CMap
    blob); new plist and quick-xml 0.42 (MIT) are macOS-only,
    webpki-root-certs 1.0.10 is not linked on Linux. License tag
    unchanged, MSRV still 1.95, no new system deps; cargo_vendor:
    "All lockfiles are audited", no RUSTSEC advisories.
- Rebase pdfcraft-no-brand-assets.patch onto 0.13.0 (hunk moved 10
  lines, same three docs/brand include_bytes! embeds; the 0.13.0
  tree has no new docs/brand references).
- Ship the licence texts of the assets the vendored hayro crates
  embed (Foxit fonts, CGATS ICC profile, Adobe CMaps) under
  pdf-backend/; list hayro-cmap and vello_common in the
  Legal-Review-Notice.

